WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.272
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.542 --> 00:10.135
Thank you so much.

3
00:10.135 --> 00:14.640
Now, I have good news and bad news for you today.

4
00:14.640 --> 00:17.643
- Which do you want first? - The good news first!

5
00:17.643 --> 00:18.519
- The good news? - Yes, sir.

6
00:18.519 --> 00:19.478
All right.

7
00:19.478 --> 00:24.274
The division commander, in recognition of our company's hard work during training,

8
00:24.274 --> 00:27.927
is treating us to a company dinner next week!

9
00:30.500 --> 00:32.199
Hey, Park Min Seok.

10
00:32.199 --> 00:33.667
Did you talk to your dad?

11
00:33.667 --> 00:35.876
No.

12
00:35.876 --> 00:37.334
Call him and say thank you.

13
00:37.334 --> 00:39.248
- Yes, I will. - Thank you.

14
00:39.248 --> 00:41.291
- Will there be meat? - Will there be alcohol, too?

15
00:41.291 --> 00:44.110
What's a company dinner without meat and booze?

16
00:45.125 --> 00:47.130
Isn't this dinner really to celebrate your promotion, Company Commander,

17
00:47.130 --> 00:50.417
rather than our hard work in the Hoguk Exercise?

18
00:50.417 --> 00:56.223
Then I'll pay for a case of PX soju that day.

19
00:56.223 --> 00:58.124
Thank you.

20
00:58.834 --> 01:00.375
Cho Baek Ho!

21
01:00.375 --> 01:06.375
- Cho Baek Ho! - Cho Baek Ho!

22
01:07.334 --> 01:10.641
Unit, attention!

23
01:12.114 --> 01:16.631
South Korea's security is now in Captain Oh Seok Jin's hands.

24
01:17.953 --> 01:21.290
Captain Oh Seok Jin!

25
01:21.290 --> 01:23.709
I'll lay down my life.

26
01:23.709 --> 01:25.043
- That's enough. - Cho Baek Ho!

27
01:25.043 --> 01:26.587
Stop!

28
01:26.587 --> 01:27.820
Hey!

29
01:27.820 --> 01:30.674
Company Commander, what's the bad news?

30
01:30.674 --> 01:32.134
The bad news?

31
01:32.134 --> 01:37.431
That dreaded week of base maintenance starts today.

32
01:37.431 --> 01:38.974
The base was empty during the Hoguk exercise.

33
01:38.974 --> 01:41.435
Let's get the whole place in shape. Okay?

34
01:41.435 --> 01:43.020
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

35
01:43.020 --> 01:45.022
Our company dinner is coming up soon.

36
01:45.022 --> 01:47.649
Let's use that excitement to get through this. All right?

37
01:47.649 --> 01:49.192
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

38
01:49.192 --> 01:51.387
Yeah. Sang Hun and Dong Woo,

39
01:51.387 --> 01:54.114
pass this on to the squad leaders in the other barracks. Okay?

40
01:54.114 --> 01:55.115
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

41
01:55.115 --> 01:56.658
Everyone, to your posts!

42
01:56.658 --> 01:59.185
- To your posts! - To your posts!

43
01:59.995 --> 02:01.797
Did you hear me?

44
02:03.540 --> 02:04.918
Seok Jin.

45
02:04.918 --> 02:08.170
Huh? Captain Oh Seok Jin!

46
02:08.170 --> 02:11.089
Captain?

47
02:11.089 --> 02:12.215
Did you get promoted to captain?

48
02:12.215 --> 02:16.511
I meant I'd work even harder to make captain.

49
02:16.511 --> 02:19.014
Oh, you were daydreaming again.

50
02:19.014 --> 02:21.433
- No. - Did you get promoted too

51
02:21.433 --> 02:22.876
because the Company Commander did?

52
02:22.876 --> 02:24.394
No, that's...

53
02:24.394 --> 02:27.292
Then I'm Sergeant Major Park Jae Su!

54
02:27.292 --> 02:28.899
Master Sergeant Im Seong Min!

55
02:28.899 --> 02:30.334
Sergeant First Class Choi Il Gu!

56
02:30.334 --> 02:32.250
Sergeant Park Min Seok!

57
02:32.250 --> 02:36.198
I'll go ahead and get ready for the maintenance work.

58
02:36.198 --> 02:38.283
Congratulations, Company Commander.

59
02:38.283 --> 02:40.077
- Hey, let's go. - Yes, sir.

60
02:40.077 --> 02:41.828
- Take it to the Company Commander's office. - Yes, sir.

61
02:41.828 --> 02:43.751
- Let's go. - Sergeant Major Choi Il Gu!

62
02:43.751 --> 02:46.537
- Captain Oh. - Captain Oh.

63
02:56.677 --> 02:59.471
[Major-select Cho Baek Ho]

64
02:59.471 --> 03:02.849
Hey, there's a line right here.

65
03:02.849 --> 03:04.309
Can't you cut along it?

66
03:04.309 --> 03:05.310
Huh?

67
03:05.310 --> 03:09.231
[EP 11. Major-select Cho Baek Ho] Why do you mess up everything you do?

68
03:09.231 --> 03:11.002
Seriously.

69
03:12.542 --> 03:13.959
You sure look busy.

70
03:13.959 --> 03:15.028
Chungseong! Love you!

71
03:15.028 --> 03:16.363
Yeah, love you too.

72
03:16.363 --> 03:18.417
Congratulations on your promotion.

73
03:18.417 --> 03:20.125
Congratulations.

74
03:20.125 --> 03:22.292
Thanks. What's all this, though?

75
03:22.292 --> 03:24.125
[Company commander, Major-select Cho Baek Ho] We're relabeling

76
03:24.125 --> 03:26.248
all your gear "Major-select"

77
03:26.248 --> 03:28.292
to reflect your promotion.

78
03:28.292 --> 03:30.836
You even thought of this?

79
03:30.836 --> 03:32.045
You're Mr. Meticulous.

80
03:32.045 --> 03:33.338
Thank you, sir.

81
03:33.338 --> 03:35.499
What a waste of tape.

82
03:36.751 --> 03:38.167
But I do appreciate it.

83
03:38.167 --> 03:40.095
It's nothing, sir.

84
03:40.095 --> 03:41.930
- Hee Jeong. - Corporal No Hee Jeong.

85
03:41.930 --> 03:44.375
They've requested someone for tennis duty this weekend

86
03:44.375 --> 03:45.809
and someone to transfer to the kitchen.

87
03:45.809 --> 03:47.728
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu is handling the cook position.

88
03:47.728 --> 03:50.000
Could you please...

89
03:50.000 --> 03:51.648
get me out of tennis duty?

90
03:51.648 --> 03:54.776
If you could just tell them we're busy with company work...

91
03:54.776 --> 03:55.959
What can I do?

92
03:55.959 --> 03:58.530
The guy there must like you. He keeps asking for you.

93
03:58.530 --> 04:00.803
Please, I'll even do company work on weekends.

94
04:00.803 --> 04:01.992
Can't you keep me here?

95
04:01.992 --> 04:04.578
I hear they're short-staffed at division headquarters.

96
04:04.578 --> 04:09.082
Without extra help, they can't take leave or get overnight or day passes.

97
04:09.082 --> 04:10.667
It's a mess over there.

98
04:10.667 --> 04:12.532
Just shut up.

99
04:13.170 --> 04:14.463
Company Commander, please.

100
04:14.463 --> 04:16.834
I really can't do tennis duty.

101
04:16.834 --> 04:18.209
All right.

102
04:18.209 --> 04:19.751
- I mean it. - All right.

103
04:19.751 --> 04:23.555
- I mean it. - All right, I won't send you.

104
04:23.555 --> 04:24.973
Company Commander.

105
04:24.973 --> 04:26.141
Chungseong! Love you!

106
04:26.141 --> 04:28.268
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri. I'm here on business at the admin office.

107
04:28.268 --> 04:29.936
Are you here about becoming a cook?

108
04:29.936 --> 04:31.229
No, sir.

109
04:31.229 --> 04:34.024
I want to stay in this company forever.

110
04:34.024 --> 04:36.109
He's clearly meant to be a cook,

111
04:36.109 --> 04:38.779
but he insists he's a combat soldier and refuses to transfer.

112
04:38.779 --> 04:40.906
Yet he's always happy to volunteer for kitchen duty.

113
04:40.906 --> 04:42.949
We can't force him to go if he doesn't want to.

114
04:42.949 --> 04:44.576
But if we don't send him,

115
04:44.576 --> 04:47.329
won't I keep getting called in by the kitchen supervisor?

116
04:47.329 --> 04:50.499
Another company will send someone, so don't worry.

117
04:50.499 --> 04:51.917
Thanks for staying, Moon Bit Na Ri.

118
04:51.917 --> 04:53.959
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! Thank you, sir.

119
04:53.959 --> 04:56.797
Just try volunteering for kitchen duty one more time.

120
04:56.797 --> 04:57.881
You'll answer to me.

121
04:57.881 --> 05:01.083
All right, shall we get started on the laundry?

122
05:01.083 --> 05:04.429
- Do you mean washing the blankets? - Yeah.

123
05:04.429 --> 05:05.931
- Today? - Yeah.

124
05:05.931 --> 05:09.918
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! I'm great with washing machines.

125
05:09.918 --> 05:11.228
That's not how we're washing them.

126
05:11.228 --> 05:14.139
Yes, I'll get things started.

127
05:17.251 --> 05:18.694
[Drying Room] Hey, is everyone here?

128
05:18.694 --> 05:21.197
Corporal Kim Dong Woo. Se Gye couldn't come because he's on duty.

129
05:21.197 --> 05:22.573
Everyone else seems to be here.

130
05:22.573 --> 05:24.543
Fine, tell him to get lost.

131
05:24.543 --> 05:26.452
Here's how you wash blankets.

132
05:26.452 --> 05:28.412
Throw them in a rubber tub,

133
05:28.412 --> 05:30.080
and dump in a ton of detergent.

134
05:30.080 --> 05:32.374
Then picture someone you've wanted to stomp on since you enlisted,

135
05:32.374 --> 05:34.918
and stomp on them as hard as you can.

136
05:34.918 --> 05:37.254
If you ask, "Can I picture you while I stomp?"

137
05:37.254 --> 05:39.173
you're dead, Park Min Seok.

138
05:39.173 --> 05:42.218
How did you know that?

139
05:42.218 --> 05:45.304
This is the first time I've seen anyone wash blankets since I enlisted.

140
05:45.304 --> 05:47.723
I only did it once when I was a private.

141
05:47.723 --> 05:51.602
They made a huge fuss about how the blankets hadn't been washed in ten years...

142
05:51.602 --> 05:53.938
But no matter how much we washed them,

143
05:53.938 --> 05:56.381
dark soy sauce kept coming out.

144
05:57.084 --> 05:59.918
How could soy sauce come out of a blanket?

145
05:59.918 --> 06:01.779
- Stop making things up. - You're such a liar.

146
06:01.779 --> 06:03.072
I'm serious.

147
06:03.072 --> 06:05.334
I haven't eaten soy-marinated crab since then.

148
06:05.334 --> 06:07.851
It reminds me of washing those blankets.

149
06:08.536 --> 06:10.329
I'm sure you'd have no trouble eating it.

150
06:10.329 --> 06:12.248
Stop!

151
06:12.248 --> 06:13.668
You always pick on me...

152
06:13.668 --> 06:14.835
Shut up.

153
06:14.835 --> 06:18.337
Anyway, Kim Sang Hun, you're in charge here.

154
06:18.337 --> 06:20.297
Turn that dark soy sauce into mineral water.

155
06:20.297 --> 06:22.716
- I'm out of here. - What do you mean?

156
06:22.716 --> 06:24.468
You're supposed to do this with us.

157
06:24.468 --> 06:27.084
I've got a bunch of work details to supervise.

158
06:27.084 --> 06:29.293
The higher-ups keep dumping work on me.

159
06:29.293 --> 06:31.945
I'm just a lowly rookie staff sergeant.

160
06:33.501 --> 06:35.271
Wait. Yes, First Sergeant.

161
06:35.271 --> 06:37.251
I'll be right there.

162
06:37.251 --> 06:38.941
Take care, sir. Chungseong! Love you!

163
06:38.941 --> 06:41.151
- He's faking it. - Understood.

164
06:41.151 --> 06:42.778
He's definitely faking it.

165
06:42.778 --> 06:45.239
Okay. Then let's get this done fast.

166
06:45.239 --> 06:46.323
Okay.

167
06:46.323 --> 06:48.334
Have you all picked a face to stomp on?

168
06:48.334 --> 06:49.334
- We have. - Yes.

169
06:49.334 --> 06:51.662
Okay. Work in pairs. Get started!

170
06:51.662 --> 06:52.793
- Get started! - Get started!

171
06:52.793 --> 06:55.982
Put it there and mix in plenty of detergent.

172
06:56.750 --> 06:57.835
That's too much.

173
06:57.835 --> 06:59.293
Hey.

174
06:59.293 --> 07:01.293
- Hey. - Hey.

175
07:01.293 --> 07:02.793
Hey, what's wrong?

176
07:02.793 --> 07:05.492
- I'll start stomping. - Start stomping.

177
07:08.418 --> 07:09.459
Oh, this feels weird.

178
07:09.459 --> 07:10.973
The color kind of reminds me of Milkis.

179
07:10.973 --> 07:13.208
Stomp harder.

180
07:15.293 --> 07:16.770
- Oh, look at that color. - This is exhausting.

181
07:16.770 --> 07:18.981
Corporal Ji Jeong Min, who are you picturing as you stomp?

182
07:18.981 --> 07:20.709
Corporal Kim Dong Woo.

183
07:22.109 --> 07:24.251
You're splashing everywhere!

184
07:24.251 --> 07:26.113
Hey, you're splashing, Moon Bit Na Ri!

185
07:26.113 --> 07:27.668
It's a secret.

186
07:27.668 --> 07:29.783
Die!

187
07:29.783 --> 07:31.209
Careful!

188
07:31.209 --> 07:33.120
You're going to fall. Watch out.

189
07:33.120 --> 07:35.042
Hey, count together.

190
07:35.042 --> 07:36.248
One, two.

191
07:36.248 --> 07:42.671
- One, two. - One, two.

192
07:42.671 --> 07:43.751
Did you wash your feet?

193
07:43.751 --> 07:46.793
Huh? Why is the water this color?

194
07:46.793 --> 07:47.843
What is this?

195
07:47.843 --> 07:49.637
Min Seok, is this because you didn't wash your feet?

196
07:49.637 --> 07:50.638
No.

197
07:50.638 --> 07:51.972
Da Hye, didn't you wash your feet?

198
07:51.972 --> 07:54.126
I did.

199
07:54.126 --> 07:56.810
The water really does look like dark soy sauce.

200
07:56.810 --> 07:57.918
Change the water.

201
07:57.918 --> 08:00.713
- Change the water. - Dump all that water out.

202
08:01.918 --> 08:03.150
I think you can start stomping now.

203
08:03.150 --> 08:05.835
[30 minutes later]

204
08:05.835 --> 08:07.613
Hey, why are you spraying me?

205
08:07.613 --> 08:09.001
I'm sorry.

206
08:09.001 --> 08:11.700
- Spray the blanket, not me. - I'm sorry.

207
08:11.700 --> 08:16.441
The water stays dirty no matter how much clean water we add.

208
08:17.747 --> 08:19.750
[An hour later] When will the water finally run clear?

209
08:19.750 --> 08:21.668
My calves feel like they're about to burst.

210
08:21.668 --> 08:23.669
Corporal Im Da Hye. Shall we switch?

211
08:23.669 --> 08:26.447
- Let's switch. - My feet are all wrinkled.

212
08:32.756 --> 08:34.251
Hey.

213
08:34.251 --> 08:36.225
Get in the tub and make up.

214
08:36.225 --> 08:38.293
[Two hours later]

215
08:38.293 --> 08:40.992
[Three hours later]

216
08:41.959 --> 08:44.918
How many times have we changed the water?

217
08:44.918 --> 08:46.151
We've changed it 18 times.

218
08:46.151 --> 08:47.668
My toes have shriveled up.

219
08:47.668 --> 08:49.418
Are we pickling our legs or what?

220
08:49.418 --> 08:52.626
My legs really have a mind of their own.

221
08:52.626 --> 08:54.042
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

222
08:54.042 --> 08:55.869
This feels like a 20-kilometer march.

223
08:55.869 --> 08:57.871
My legs just keep moving on their own.

224
08:57.871 --> 09:01.810
Come on, why won't this end?

225
09:04.209 --> 09:05.711
All right, twist it.

226
09:07.126 --> 09:08.132
Twist it again.

227
09:08.132 --> 09:10.001
One, two, three.

228
09:10.001 --> 09:12.418
You can't twist it the same way I am.

229
09:12.418 --> 09:13.315
Okay.

230
09:13.315 --> 09:15.626
Why is so much water coming out of yours?

231
09:15.626 --> 09:17.141
Park Min Seok, you're good at this, huh?

232
09:17.141 --> 09:19.509
Did you even stomp on this properly?

233
09:20.728 --> 09:21.812
Ow, my shoulders.

234
09:21.812 --> 09:23.480
You guys are done. Hurry up and hang them up.

235
09:23.480 --> 09:24.732
- Understood. - Understood.

236
09:24.732 --> 09:27.026
- Isn't this good enough? - It's done. Hang it up.

237
09:27.026 --> 09:29.042
- Understood. - Understood.

238
09:29.042 --> 09:31.376
Next time, I'll suggest we just air them out first.

239
09:31.376 --> 09:33.168
What are we even doing?

240
09:33.168 --> 09:35.042
Okay.

241
09:35.042 --> 09:37.001
It looks like we're finally done.

242
09:37.001 --> 09:38.454
That gave my biceps a great workout.

243
09:38.454 --> 09:40.456
- Moon Bit Na Ri. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

244
09:40.456 --> 09:42.791
Loud and clear! Shout it!

245
09:42.791 --> 09:46.673
We're done washing the blankets!

246
09:49.215 --> 09:51.050
- Thanks for your hard work. - Good job, guys. Grab the tub.

247
09:51.050 --> 09:53.543
- Thanks for your hard work. - Let's head inside and get some rest too.

248
09:53.543 --> 09:55.589
- Okay. - Okay.

249
09:56.346 --> 09:57.514
Min Seok, are you okay?

250
09:57.514 --> 09:59.643
Yes, I'm okay.

251
10:09.877 --> 10:11.612
What do we do?

252
10:11.612 --> 10:13.501
Quick, put it back in.

253
10:13.501 --> 10:16.265
You should've hung it up properly.

254
10:20.746 --> 10:22.498
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong.

255
10:22.498 --> 10:24.542
Today's spicy pork was delicious.

256
10:24.542 --> 10:25.793
- The pork was pretty good, right? - Yes.

257
10:25.793 --> 10:27.084
I put some extra effort into it.

258
10:27.084 --> 10:30.964
I don't know why we're washing blankets with our feet when we have washing machines.

259
10:30.964 --> 10:32.174
I'm hungry.

260
10:32.174 --> 10:34.301
- Hey, Moon Bit Na Ri. - Huh?

261
10:34.301 --> 10:36.751
What brings you all the way here?

262
10:36.751 --> 10:38.972
You know I don't ask for favors often.

263
10:38.972 --> 10:41.334
- Come on, be a cook. - No, I can't.

264
10:41.334 --> 10:43.543
Did you come all this way just to ask me that?

265
10:43.543 --> 10:46.042
You were born to be a cook.

266
10:46.042 --> 10:48.524
I realized something after our last exercise.

267
10:48.524 --> 10:51.126
I'm definitely cut out for combat.

268
10:51.126 --> 10:52.528
Combat? Please.

269
10:52.528 --> 10:54.113
You're a born cook.

270
10:54.113 --> 10:55.168
No, I'm not.

271
10:55.168 --> 10:57.241
I've been watching you for a long time.

272
10:57.241 --> 10:59.743
You clean your plate three times a day.

273
10:59.743 --> 11:03.104
If you become a cook, you can eat great food every day.

274
11:07.668 --> 11:09.420
What kind of food do you mean?

275
11:09.420 --> 11:11.418
Just wait.

276
11:11.418 --> 11:12.422
Ta-da!

277
11:12.422 --> 11:15.418
Isn't that just hardtack?

278
11:15.418 --> 11:17.422
I'm not done yet.

279
11:20.543 --> 11:22.874
You look like a professional chef.

280
11:24.918 --> 11:26.001
Fill it up, please.

281
11:26.001 --> 11:29.793
The cook's breakfast special.

282
11:29.793 --> 11:32.216
- Try it. - Thank you.

283
11:44.793 --> 11:46.328
Oh, strawberry milk.

284
11:46.328 --> 11:47.334
How is it?

285
11:47.334 --> 11:49.007
Do you want to be a cook?

286
11:50.710 --> 11:53.334
I'm still not sure.

287
11:53.334 --> 11:55.418
Well then...

288
11:55.418 --> 11:56.508
Ta-da!

289
11:56.508 --> 11:58.301
And here...

290
11:59.543 --> 12:02.804
Military French toast.

291
12:04.084 --> 12:05.459
Try it with strawberry jam.

292
12:05.459 --> 12:07.019
Okay.

293
12:07.019 --> 12:08.803
Strawberry jam.

294
12:18.793 --> 12:20.312
This is good.

295
12:23.459 --> 12:25.436
It's delicious.

296
12:26.038 --> 12:27.080
It's amazing, right?

297
12:27.080 --> 12:29.041
I need to eat this regularly.

298
12:30.168 --> 12:32.043
It's so moist.

299
12:34.751 --> 12:36.501
That was good.

300
12:36.501 --> 12:39.784
What do you think? You can eat like this every day.

301
12:41.209 --> 12:44.209
Then, if I wanted to become a cook...

302
12:44.209 --> 12:45.835
Yeah?

303
12:45.835 --> 12:47.376
No, I can't.

304
12:47.376 --> 12:49.311
I can't betray my fellow soldiers.

305
12:49.311 --> 12:50.771
But you enjoyed it so much.

306
12:50.771 --> 12:52.731
Your appetite doesn't lie.

307
12:52.731 --> 12:53.732
No.

308
12:53.732 --> 12:59.112
I only ate because my blood sugar was low after I washed the blankets.

309
12:59.112 --> 13:00.668
Even that didn't work?

310
13:00.668 --> 13:02.130
Okay.

311
13:05.334 --> 13:07.728
This is really hard to get.

312
13:10.668 --> 13:12.084
Ta-da!

313
13:12.084 --> 13:13.543
Aren't these just rice noodles?

314
13:13.543 --> 13:14.872
The cooks' secret recipe.

315
13:14.872 --> 13:16.630
Carbonara rice noodles.

316
13:16.630 --> 13:18.993
Carbonara rice noodles?

317
13:21.084 --> 13:24.120
It really does smell like carbonara.

318
13:37.918 --> 13:39.278
Is it milk?

319
13:39.278 --> 13:40.376
It's so creamy.

320
13:40.376 --> 13:43.084
You know your stuff.

321
13:43.084 --> 13:44.074
How is it?

322
13:44.074 --> 13:46.171
It tastes just like what I ate before I enlisted.

323
13:46.171 --> 13:48.704
Now for my secret weapon.

324
13:48.704 --> 13:51.297
Is there more?

325
13:52.457 --> 13:54.293
What is that?

326
13:54.293 --> 13:56.276
My secret weapon.

327
13:58.793 --> 14:01.084
Oh, this is...

328
14:01.084 --> 14:03.927
Fried eggs even veteran sergeants can't get their hands on,

329
14:03.927 --> 14:06.651
plus some oxtail soup I stashed away.

330
14:09.349 --> 14:12.241
- Oh, meat. - It's full of meat.

331
14:12.241 --> 14:15.098
That's a perk of being a cook.

332
14:15.098 --> 14:16.440
Dig in.

333
14:16.440 --> 14:17.999
Thank you.

334
14:24.656 --> 14:26.885
The meat is really good.

335
14:28.710 --> 14:29.918
What do you think?

336
14:29.918 --> 14:33.168
Cooks get to eat like this every day.

337
14:33.168 --> 14:34.251
Give it a try.

338
14:34.251 --> 14:36.251
All right.

339
14:36.251 --> 14:39.918
But you have to promise I can eat like this every day.

340
14:39.918 --> 14:41.006
Of course.

341
14:41.006 --> 14:42.924
- You're becoming a cook, right? - Sounds good.

342
14:42.924 --> 14:44.365
Okay.

343
14:45.761 --> 14:47.710
Bit Na Ri says he'll be a cook.

344
14:47.710 --> 14:49.723
- Bit Na Ri says he'll be a cook. - It's not final yet.

345
14:49.723 --> 14:52.126
Bit Na Ri says he'll be a cook.

346
14:52.126 --> 14:53.585
Why are you doing this?

347
14:53.585 --> 14:56.521
We were just talking in private. How can you tell everyone like that?

348
14:56.521 --> 14:57.814
Chungseong! Love you!

349
14:57.814 --> 15:00.266
I was going to think it over later.

350
15:06.949 --> 15:09.534
Didn't you say you wouldn't do it?

351
15:09.534 --> 15:12.938
I'm sorry. I got distracted by the food...

352
15:13.644 --> 15:14.664
Hey.

353
15:14.664 --> 15:16.501
Yes, sir...

354
15:16.501 --> 15:18.084
Go and make some spicy beef soup.

355
15:18.084 --> 15:19.751
There's going to be a funeral.

356
15:19.751 --> 15:21.710
Understood.

357
15:21.710 --> 15:23.959
I'll pick up the tray later.

358
15:23.959 --> 15:27.719
You must've forgotten what I'm like.

359
15:27.719 --> 15:29.679
I'm sorry.

360
15:29.679 --> 15:31.751
I'm really sorry.

361
15:31.751 --> 15:33.809
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu. - What?

362
15:33.809 --> 15:39.398
If I'm going to die anyway, can I at least have some oxtail soup?

363
15:39.398 --> 15:42.042
Are you crazy?

364
15:42.042 --> 15:44.736
You repay my kindness by betraying me?

365
15:44.736 --> 15:46.057
I tap out!

366
15:46.057 --> 15:47.073
Are you crazy?

367
15:47.073 --> 15:49.169
I tap out!

368
15:51.284 --> 15:52.793
I'm full.

369
15:52.793 --> 15:54.538
How about some adlay tea and a smoke?

370
15:54.538 --> 15:56.373
- Sounds good. - Sounds good.

371
15:56.373 --> 15:59.442
Park Min Seok, you brought change, right?

372
16:02.003 --> 16:03.251
I don't have any.

373
16:03.251 --> 16:05.674
You never carry any change.

374
16:05.674 --> 16:07.126
I'm always paying for the guys.

375
16:07.126 --> 16:08.635
That's why I'm out of change.

376
16:08.635 --> 16:11.209
Yeah, right.

377
16:11.209 --> 16:12.418
Hey.

378
16:12.418 --> 16:14.015
Corporal Park Min Seok. Thank you.

379
16:14.015 --> 16:15.621
Thank you.

380
16:17.769 --> 16:19.628
[Adlay Tea]

381
16:23.293 --> 16:24.818
What are you doing? Hurry up and press the button.

382
16:24.818 --> 16:29.823
But don't they say adlay tea is bad for men?

383
16:29.823 --> 16:31.668
Do you actually believe that stuff?

384
16:31.668 --> 16:33.160
It's not like you're getting any action.

385
16:33.160 --> 16:35.287
Just drink it already.

386
16:35.287 --> 16:36.930
Okay.

387
16:42.169 --> 16:43.170
Wait.

388
16:43.170 --> 16:44.793
I'll have coffee.

389
16:44.793 --> 16:46.835
Why aren't you having adlay tea?

390
16:46.835 --> 16:48.959
I'd rather not risk it.

391
16:48.959 --> 16:50.502
It's ready.

392
16:52.418 --> 16:54.512
Then I'll have coffee too.

393
16:55.098 --> 16:56.558
What?

394
16:56.558 --> 16:59.418
It's not fair that I'm the only one stuck drinking adlay tea.

395
16:59.418 --> 17:02.710
This is what's really unfair.

396
17:02.710 --> 17:04.294
What?

397
17:06.209 --> 17:07.736
Look at your face.

398
17:07.736 --> 17:10.822
You look like you're thinking, "Serves you right for being mean."

399
17:10.822 --> 17:13.751
No. Absolutely not.

400
17:13.751 --> 17:15.494
Why is this thing acting up?

401
17:15.494 --> 17:18.168
Hey! What are you doing?

402
17:18.168 --> 17:20.543
If you mess with that and break it,

403
17:20.543 --> 17:23.959
you'll be in big trouble, Division Commander's son or not.

404
17:23.959 --> 17:25.668
Sorry, what was that?

405
17:25.668 --> 17:27.923
You still have a lot to learn.

406
17:27.923 --> 17:30.550
Who are the two all-powerful civilians

407
17:30.550 --> 17:33.751
who can walk right through our main gate?

408
17:33.751 --> 17:35.013
Civilians?

409
17:35.013 --> 17:37.224
The guy who collects food scraps

410
17:37.224 --> 17:39.684
and the vending machine lady.

411
17:39.684 --> 17:40.710
That's right.

412
17:40.710 --> 17:42.187
Have you ever seen her?

413
17:42.187 --> 17:44.439
No, not once.

414
17:44.439 --> 17:46.751
I've seen the food scrap collector a few times, though.

415
17:46.751 --> 17:49.319
I can't believe you still haven't seen that legend.

416
17:49.319 --> 17:52.031
You've got a long way to go.

417
17:52.031 --> 17:57.668
That vending machine lady has been here since this unit was formed.

418
17:57.668 --> 17:58.745
Really?

419
17:58.745 --> 18:01.623
They say she turned every officer's head in her prime,

420
18:01.623 --> 18:04.251
from the regimental commander

421
18:04.251 --> 18:07.212
down to the greenest second lieutenant.

422
18:07.212 --> 18:10.085
She was a legendary femme fatale

423
18:10.085 --> 18:13.418
who stole every officer's heart.

424
18:13.418 --> 18:15.603
Oh, a femme fatale.

425
18:35.959 --> 18:38.209
Vending Machine Jung, are you here?

426
18:38.209 --> 18:41.580
I changed this month's entire paycheck into 100-won coins.

427
18:41.580 --> 18:43.415
I'm spending it all on vending machine coffee.

428
18:43.415 --> 18:44.791
Move over, man.

429
18:44.791 --> 18:48.461
I changed my entire paycheck and even my allowances into 100-won coins.

430
18:48.461 --> 18:50.746
What do you think? Isn't that cool?

431
18:53.959 --> 18:56.196
Thank you, everyone.

432
18:56.196 --> 18:58.471
Training's tough today, isn't it?

433
18:58.471 --> 19:02.583
When you need a sugar boost, nothing beats coffee from this machine.

434
19:04.227 --> 19:07.731
Get yourselves plenty of coffee.

435
19:10.859 --> 19:14.821
- Thanks for the coffee! - Thanks for the coffee!

436
19:14.821 --> 19:18.992
They say one smile had the whole unit under her spell.

437
19:18.992 --> 19:22.001
"When you need a sugar boost, nothing beats vending machine coffee."

438
19:22.001 --> 19:24.980
"Get yourselves plenty of coffee."

439
19:26.417 --> 19:30.171
What's the one rule when you get coffee for the First Sergeant?

440
19:30.171 --> 19:34.007
Never pick the first coffee option.

441
19:34.007 --> 19:36.001
Right. Do you know why?

442
19:36.001 --> 19:38.959
This is the first I've heard of that.

443
19:38.959 --> 19:41.413
Well, it's...

444
19:47.521 --> 19:50.510
Hey, Vending Machine Jung.

445
19:51.483 --> 19:52.693
Oh, you're here.

446
19:52.693 --> 19:58.531
My love for you is like this fiery red rose.

447
19:58.531 --> 20:02.243
This rain falls to bring you,

448
20:02.243 --> 20:05.187
a red rose, into full bloom.

449
20:06.376 --> 20:11.731
Will you visit my family back home with me next week?

450
20:13.668 --> 20:15.883
This is driving me crazy.

451
20:15.883 --> 20:17.751
This is why I'm so exhausted.

452
20:17.751 --> 20:20.459
You only drink black coffee,

453
20:20.459 --> 20:22.971
but why aren't you nice?

454
20:23.835 --> 20:26.231
What do you mean?

455
20:27.686 --> 20:29.312
Listen, Jae Su.

456
20:29.312 --> 20:31.398
To me,

457
20:31.398 --> 20:33.400
love is like a vending machine.

458
20:33.400 --> 20:34.859
Look at this.

459
20:34.859 --> 20:38.154
If this one's you, then this one's Mr. Kim.

460
20:38.154 --> 20:40.615
This one's Captain Choi, this one's Mr. Park, and so on.

461
20:40.615 --> 20:42.126
Do you get it?

462
20:42.126 --> 20:45.620
I can't be devoted to just one man.

463
20:45.620 --> 20:48.188
That's how I'll live for the rest of my life.

464
21:00.427 --> 21:01.418
"If this one's Jae Su..."

465
21:01.418 --> 21:04.681
If this one's Jae Su, this one's Captain Choi, and so on.

466
21:04.681 --> 21:06.933
"My love is like a vending machine."

467
21:06.933 --> 21:09.686
"That's how I'll live for the rest of my life."

468
21:09.686 --> 21:12.689
That's why he still can't bring himself to press that button.

469
21:12.689 --> 21:17.402
I really want to see for myself just how beautiful she is.

470
21:17.402 --> 21:19.237
Come on, how could that be true?

471
21:19.237 --> 21:20.905
I'm telling you, it's true.

472
21:20.905 --> 21:22.198
Don't you know how army stories work?

473
21:22.198 --> 21:25.702
The believable ones are fake, and the unbelievable ones are true.

474
21:25.702 --> 21:30.939
Why else would that rule get passed down to whoever gets the First Sergeant's coffee?

475
21:31.877 --> 21:33.585
Let's go for a smoke. Throw this away.

476
21:33.585 --> 21:35.462
- Okay. - Come on, let's go.

477
21:35.462 --> 21:38.947
But seriously, getting plain water is ridiculous.

478
21:39.710 --> 21:41.134
Leave it alone.

479
21:41.134 --> 21:42.719
Hey, cut it out.

480
21:42.719 --> 21:45.181
But other people might buy coffee from it too...

481
21:45.181 --> 21:47.626
I paid for it. Why are you making such a fuss?

482
21:47.626 --> 21:49.338
- Hey! - Hey!

483
21:50.918 --> 21:53.991
Stop!

484
21:55.334 --> 21:58.126
What are you doing? I'll snap your wrist.

485
21:58.126 --> 22:00.236
- Who are you? - And who are you?

486
22:00.236 --> 22:01.334
Corporal Park Min Seok...

487
22:01.334 --> 22:03.823
Do you want your army career to end as a corporal?

488
22:03.823 --> 22:05.385
No...

489
22:07.493 --> 22:08.745
She's the...

490
22:08.745 --> 22:10.121
Hello, ma'am.

491
22:10.121 --> 22:11.877
"Ma'am?"

492
22:11.877 --> 22:13.416
Hello, Auntie.

493
22:13.416 --> 22:15.585
"Auntie?"

494
22:15.585 --> 22:17.086
Hello, miss.

495
22:17.086 --> 22:18.254
Here's the thing.

496
22:18.254 --> 22:20.799
I paid for coffee, but all I got was plain water.

497
22:20.799 --> 22:22.251
Are you kidding me?

498
22:22.251 --> 22:23.301
Well, well.

499
22:23.301 --> 22:25.470
I've got you now, you coin thief.

500
22:25.470 --> 22:27.001
You're in for it now.

501
22:27.001 --> 22:30.016
It wasn't me. Those coins...

502
22:30.016 --> 22:31.918
Step aside.

503
22:31.918 --> 22:34.545
Oh, my sweet Yi Rang!

504
22:36.732 --> 22:39.543
What's got you so upset?

505
22:39.543 --> 22:40.610
Park Min Seok.

506
22:40.610 --> 22:42.209
Oh, you're here.

507
22:42.209 --> 22:43.793
Why did you take your watch off?

508
22:43.793 --> 22:45.657
Oh, no. It's nothing.

509
22:45.657 --> 22:47.585
Maybe my wrist's gotten thinner. What's wrong with this thing?

510
22:47.585 --> 22:50.084
I told you I'd buy you a watch.

511
22:50.084 --> 22:52.334
No, that's okay.

512
22:52.334 --> 22:55.334
But have you lost some weight?

513
22:55.334 --> 22:56.334
You're looking good.

514
22:56.334 --> 22:57.585
My belly's gotten a little smaller.

515
22:57.585 --> 22:58.835
Have you been hauling a lot of food scraps?

516
22:58.835 --> 23:04.209
I'd rather find a scrap of time to see you than collect food scraps.

517
23:04.209 --> 23:06.399
Oh, you.

518
23:08.096 --> 23:09.597
Yi Rang.

519
23:09.597 --> 23:14.710
Could I have my usual coffee?

520
23:16.939 --> 23:21.751
You still won't give me a chance?

521
23:21.751 --> 23:23.736
There you go again.

522
23:23.736 --> 23:27.156
Haven't I told you this over and over?

523
23:27.156 --> 23:30.994
To me, love is like a vending machine.

524
23:30.994 --> 23:33.456
That's what I was telling you about.

525
23:33.456 --> 23:35.331
You're so aloof.

526
23:35.331 --> 23:40.077
Am I the only one who can barely stand this?

527
23:41.004 --> 23:43.626
This feels worse than tear gas training.

528
23:43.626 --> 23:45.592
Yeah, this is hard to watch.

529
23:45.592 --> 23:46.968
Park Min Seok!

530
23:46.968 --> 23:48.344
Corporal Park Min Seok.

531
23:48.344 --> 23:49.762
Get your head on straight!

532
23:49.762 --> 23:51.668
Yes, I understand.

533
23:51.668 --> 23:53.224
You're so cute. Why are you acting like this?

534
23:53.224 --> 23:55.668
Thank you.

535
23:55.668 --> 23:57.585
Let's go.

536
23:57.585 --> 23:59.564
- Don't wear a wig. - Goodbye.

537
23:59.564 --> 24:01.710
But I look better with a wig.

538
24:01.710 --> 24:03.293
True, but don't.

539
24:03.293 --> 24:04.736
Wait.

540
24:04.736 --> 24:07.251
I need to get something ready with the assistant platoon leader.

541
24:07.251 --> 24:09.032
I'll head out first.

542
24:09.032 --> 24:11.241
- Understood. - Understood.

543
24:12.796 --> 24:14.997
Hello, sir.

544
24:14.997 --> 24:18.317
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

545
24:20.585 --> 24:22.404
Hurry up!

546
24:23.084 --> 24:25.322
Come on, hurry!

547
24:45.610 --> 24:47.293
Congratulations, Second Company Commander.

548
24:47.293 --> 24:48.488
Thank you.

549
24:48.488 --> 24:49.697
I owe it to you, sir.

550
24:49.697 --> 24:51.825
Oh, I hardly did anything.

551
24:51.825 --> 24:56.704
You've earned this through years of quiet perseverance and hard work.

552
24:56.704 --> 24:58.289
It came a little late, though.

553
24:58.289 --> 25:01.501
Honestly, I wasn't expecting much, but it felt good.

554
25:01.501 --> 25:04.069
Of course. It's something to be happy about.

555
25:07.383 --> 25:09.604
Now it's time to prepare

556
25:09.604 --> 25:12.319
for the responsibilities of a field-grade officer.

557
25:12.929 --> 25:17.934
I hope you'll start looking out for yourself more,

558
25:17.934 --> 25:23.023
instead of putting the soldiers first like you used to.

559
25:23.023 --> 25:25.483
Yes, I'll keep that in mind.

560
25:25.483 --> 25:27.652
And as you know,

561
25:27.652 --> 25:31.698
you need to be extra careful about everything you say and do.

562
25:31.698 --> 25:34.450
Caution isn't just for sergeants near discharge.

563
25:34.450 --> 25:37.662
A major-select needs to be careful too.

564
25:37.662 --> 25:39.447
Yes, I understand.

565
25:40.748 --> 25:42.583
The company dinner's next week, right?

566
25:42.583 --> 25:44.751
Yes. Will you be joining us too, sir?

567
25:44.751 --> 25:47.959
Let the soldiers relax and enjoy their meal.

568
25:47.959 --> 25:49.007
Yes, I understand.

569
25:49.007 --> 25:53.084
Keep an eye on things so everyone can have a good time.

570
25:53.084 --> 25:54.846
Understood.

571
25:54.846 --> 25:56.681
And this is for you.

572
25:56.681 --> 25:58.543
You don't have to.

573
25:58.543 --> 26:00.353
Please take it.

574
26:01.770 --> 26:03.279
Thank you.

575
26:04.793 --> 26:08.985
Congratulations, Second Company Commander. I mean it.

576
26:08.985 --> 26:11.112
Thank you. I really appreciate it.

577
26:11.112 --> 26:14.657
We should have a celebratory drink soon.

578
26:14.657 --> 26:18.293
Soju with ice and lemon.

579
26:18.293 --> 26:21.122
- Will the First Sergeant join us too? - Of course.

580
26:21.122 --> 26:23.065
I'll look forward to it.

581
26:24.875 --> 26:26.256
Come in.

582
26:26.877 --> 26:29.839
Chungseong. Battalion Commander, you have a visitor.

583
26:29.839 --> 26:31.457
A visitor? Who?

584
26:39.432 --> 26:41.100
Chungseong.

585
26:42.185 --> 26:44.103
What brings you here without calling ahead?

586
26:44.103 --> 26:45.688
I stopped by to see someone

587
26:45.688 --> 26:48.058
and heard there might be something to celebrate.

588
26:49.984 --> 26:52.334
- Cho Baek Ho. - Captain Cho Baek Ho.

589
26:52.334 --> 26:53.931
Congratulations.

590
26:53.931 --> 26:55.198
Thank you.

591
26:55.198 --> 26:57.474
You're a major-select now.

592
27:04.209 --> 27:08.037
You're quite something.

593
27:11.005 --> 27:13.312
You really do have talent.

594
27:15.593 --> 27:18.453
Let's get together to celebrate soon.

595
27:19.055 --> 27:20.457
Keep up the good work.

596
27:21.058 --> 27:22.267
I'm heading out.

597
27:22.267 --> 27:24.560
- Chungseong! - Yeah.

598
27:39.659 --> 27:41.244
- I'll head back now. - All right.

599
27:41.244 --> 27:44.370
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

600
27:58.010 --> 28:00.471
Yes, Operations Chief.

601
28:00.471 --> 28:04.142
I'll head over to the site now.

602
28:04.142 --> 28:05.581
Yes.

603
28:14.652 --> 28:20.128
[Battalion commander, Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin]

604
28:31.212 --> 28:32.920
I've loaded everything into the car.

605
28:32.920 --> 28:35.918
[May this youth shine for the motherland!] Oh, thank you.

606
28:35.918 --> 28:40.344
I have a good feeling I'll meet the love of my life today.

607
28:40.344 --> 28:41.596
- Hey. - Yes?

608
28:41.596 --> 28:44.918
If things work out for me, I'll treat you.

609
28:44.918 --> 28:46.376
Yes.

610
28:46.376 --> 28:48.060
I think we're going to be late.

611
28:48.060 --> 28:49.168
We should hurry.

612
28:49.168 --> 28:51.213
- Let's go. - Yes.

613
28:59.543 --> 29:00.865
- Hey. - Yes?

614
29:00.865 --> 29:02.793
There are plenty of nice campsites.

615
29:02.793 --> 29:06.144
Why are we camping on a hill near the base?

616
29:06.747 --> 29:10.583
Isn't the real fun of camping being out in the wild?

617
29:10.583 --> 29:11.709
And it's free.

618
29:11.709 --> 29:13.293
- Is that so? - Yes.

619
29:13.293 --> 29:14.962
Hey, how are they getting here?

620
29:14.962 --> 29:16.376
Did they say they're driving?

621
29:16.376 --> 29:19.469
I didn't check that.

622
29:21.260 --> 29:23.746
- Here they come. - Yes.

623
29:34.543 --> 29:37.818
Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju, what brings you here?

624
29:37.818 --> 29:39.376
Hey, what's going on?

625
29:39.376 --> 29:41.209
Well...

626
29:41.209 --> 29:43.334
I'll get straight to the point.

627
29:43.334 --> 29:46.668
I wanted to go camping with you.

628
29:46.668 --> 29:49.205
But I was worried you wouldn't come if I asked you directly,

629
29:49.205 --> 29:51.773
so I asked Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu for help.

630
29:53.125 --> 29:55.211
I'm sorry. I had no choice.

631
29:55.211 --> 29:58.071
I was afraid I might die.

632
29:58.673 --> 30:00.459
If you wanted to go camping with me,

633
30:00.459 --> 30:03.891
why didn't you just ask me directly?

634
30:03.891 --> 30:08.481
Still, it's nice to see you after such a long time.

635
30:10.793 --> 30:11.977
Yes.

636
30:11.977 --> 30:16.331
Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju, didn't you say one more person was coming?

637
30:16.331 --> 30:19.791
She's coming separately. Let's unload the gear from the car first.

638
30:19.791 --> 30:21.761
- Yes. - Yes, ma'am.

639
30:38.812 --> 30:41.154
[Min Ju, I think I'll be a little late]

640
30:42.607 --> 30:46.667
The unnie who's coming with me is running late. Let's set up the tent first.

641
30:46.667 --> 30:51.947
Yes, ma'am. Where should we set up the tent?

642
30:51.947 --> 30:55.197
Under that tree over there looks good.

643
31:06.127 --> 31:10.584
Good soil, no moisture. It's optimal for building a position.

644
31:10.584 --> 31:11.901
Let's do it here.

645
31:12.497 --> 31:18.376
There's a stream nearby and it blocks the wind. It's the perfect spot for a tent.

646
31:18.376 --> 31:21.590
Excellent choice as always, Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju.

647
31:23.747 --> 31:27.622
Men, we will establish the campsite as of now.

648
31:27.622 --> 31:30.517
- Move out! - Move out!

649
31:31.327 --> 31:33.818
- Move it, move it! - Yes, ma'am!

650
31:45.113 --> 31:47.781
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, what's this? A dog house?

651
31:47.781 --> 31:49.825
It's a one-touch tent.

652
31:49.825 --> 31:53.995
If a situation breaks out, you can pack up and leave immediately.

653
31:53.995 --> 31:57.663
- Good grief. - I'm sorry.

654
32:00.987 --> 32:05.387
Did you hear that? Was that a wild boar?

655
32:05.387 --> 32:07.817
- Step back. - Yes, ma'am.

656
32:08.587 --> 32:09.922
Oh, no.

657
32:21.147 --> 32:24.584
- Look at that. All the way here on a bike? - A bike date is a bit much.

658
32:24.584 --> 32:26.353
Min Ju!

659
32:31.807 --> 32:34.817
Seriously, Min Ju!

660
32:35.527 --> 32:38.667
Sorry. I'm a bit late, right?

661
32:38.667 --> 32:41.379
I'm a mess after that bike ride.

662
32:41.379 --> 32:43.087
Chungseong!

663
32:43.087 --> 32:46.767
Why salute out here? Just call me unnie.

664
32:46.767 --> 32:50.147
No, ma'am. You look great today.

665
32:50.147 --> 32:53.375
Is she the one who was supposed to come?

666
32:53.375 --> 32:54.627
Yes, that's right.

667
32:54.627 --> 32:58.487
Chungseong. I'm Sergeant First Class Im Seong Min.

668
32:58.487 --> 33:00.296
Chungseong. I'm Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

669
33:00.296 --> 33:02.667
I've heard a lot about you.

670
33:03.317 --> 33:06.047
- I'm Captain Kim Hye Sun. - Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

671
33:06.047 --> 33:10.227
Are you from the Poisonous Snake Unit? Or the Special Warfare Command?

672
33:10.227 --> 33:13.785
She's a nursing officer from the Academy.

673
33:13.785 --> 33:15.656
A nursing officer?

674
33:20.542 --> 33:24.671
Have we met somewhere before?

675
33:24.671 --> 33:29.887
Men usually start conversations like that. Are you hitting on me the moment we meet?

676
33:29.887 --> 33:33.567
No, no. It's not that. I really think I've seen you before.

677
33:33.567 --> 33:35.123
Are you sure?

678
33:35.123 --> 33:39.537
No. I must have been mistaken.

679
33:52.887 --> 33:54.971
Do you have any water?

680
33:54.971 --> 33:57.461
I'll go get some.

681
34:02.007 --> 34:05.879
I forgot to buy water. Hey, Il Gu! Do you have any?

682
34:05.879 --> 34:09.258
Wasn't water your responsibility?

683
34:09.258 --> 34:12.902
Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju, do you have extra water?

684
34:12.902 --> 34:17.567
- Why water? - We forgot to bring any.

685
34:17.567 --> 34:20.536
You can find water anytime, anywhere.

686
34:20.536 --> 34:22.237
What do you mean?

687
34:23.987 --> 34:28.447
Well, drinking this straight might have parasites and stuff...

688
34:28.447 --> 34:34.377
Just drink it. Or should I let the blood in your mouth wet your throat?

689
34:39.027 --> 34:40.527
Sorry.

690
34:41.607 --> 34:44.547
If there's no water, we have to drink this.

691
34:44.547 --> 34:47.837
Sergeant First Class Im, could you wait a moment?

692
34:57.787 --> 35:00.687
This is what we learned during NCO training.

693
35:00.687 --> 35:04.527
Isn't this from that show, "Survival on a Deserted Island?"

694
35:04.527 --> 35:06.027
Exactly.

695
35:10.859 --> 35:13.407
Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju, you're amazing.

696
35:13.407 --> 35:16.637
Then let me pour you a cup.

697
35:23.582 --> 35:26.345
- Isn't it so clear? - Look at this.

698
35:31.507 --> 35:33.912
- Here. - Thank you.

699
35:33.912 --> 35:35.429
Stop!

700
35:37.195 --> 35:40.682
Physical filtration is a pass. But what about biological contamination?

701
35:40.682 --> 35:41.707
Contamination?

702
35:41.707 --> 35:45.127
- Do you want typhoid, cholera, or dysentery? - No, ma'am.

703
35:45.127 --> 35:48.563
As a nursing officer responsible for your health,

704
35:48.563 --> 35:51.693
I won't allow patients on my watch.

705
35:51.693 --> 35:55.397
We'll now conduct chemical disinfection. Commence.

706
35:58.627 --> 36:01.267
Primary disinfection complete.

707
36:01.267 --> 36:07.267
Secondary boiling will kill any parasites. Sterilization complete.

708
36:09.167 --> 36:12.074
It's now perfectly sterile.

709
36:12.074 --> 36:14.327
- You may drink it with confidence. - Yes, ma'am.

710
36:14.327 --> 36:18.017
Water is also food, so drink slowly.

711
36:20.127 --> 36:22.667
This tastes like bottled water.

712
36:22.667 --> 36:24.957
Can I have a sip too?

713
36:26.847 --> 36:29.167
This precious water isn't for everyone.

714
36:29.167 --> 36:31.417
Wait, then what about me?

715
36:32.987 --> 36:34.987
How could I drink that water?

716
36:34.987 --> 36:37.727
- You won't die. - If you do, I'll save you.

717
36:37.727 --> 36:40.503
This is so unfair, really.

718
36:43.167 --> 36:44.916
This guy...

719
36:46.855 --> 36:51.575
I don't even like water. I'll just eat some parasites later. Whatever.

720
36:51.575 --> 36:55.005
Parasites are just protein anyway.

721
37:07.155 --> 37:10.225
The fire is all ready to start.

722
37:11.355 --> 37:15.605
Okay, I'll set the table. Pork belly and...

723
37:18.775 --> 37:21.135
What's that? Is it beef?

724
37:21.135 --> 37:24.595
It's a wild boar's hind leg from a roadkill during the Cheonri March last week.

725
37:24.595 --> 37:26.935
Is it okay to eat wild boar?

726
37:26.935 --> 37:28.431
This is a real delicacy.

727
37:28.431 --> 37:31.615
Wild boar is the best. Drained the blood?

728
37:31.615 --> 37:36.074
- It's me, Park Min Ju. - Good. I trust you. Let's do it.

729
37:37.295 --> 37:39.862
It wasn't roadkill, was it?

730
37:39.862 --> 37:43.375
You just killed it yourself, didn't you?

731
37:43.375 --> 37:44.541
Bingo!

732
37:45.855 --> 37:47.725
You're pretty quick-witted.

733
37:48.519 --> 37:53.055
We'll need thick logs to grill this. Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, go get some.

734
37:53.055 --> 37:56.715
- But we have a gas stove here... - Just go.

735
37:56.715 --> 37:58.565
Yes.

736
37:59.655 --> 38:03.145
Asking for logs when we have gas...

737
38:06.095 --> 38:07.845
That stings.

738
38:08.786 --> 38:11.354
It stings.

739
38:11.354 --> 38:14.267
I was a fool to expect anything.

740
38:14.915 --> 38:17.673
Should I just bolt? No.

741
38:17.673 --> 38:21.556
Im Seong Min will sulk. Petty guy.

742
38:22.155 --> 38:24.365
Let's just endure it for one day.

743
38:26.455 --> 38:28.915
I think I saw this tree earlier.

744
38:28.915 --> 38:33.115
We'll need thick logs to grill this. Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, go get some.

745
38:33.115 --> 38:36.775
- But we have a gas stove here... - Just go.

746
38:36.775 --> 38:38.545
Yes.

747
38:39.695 --> 38:43.425
Asking for logs when we have gas...

748
38:46.243 --> 38:47.981
That stings.

749
38:48.829 --> 38:51.412
It stings.

750
38:51.412 --> 38:54.335
I was a fool to expect anything.

751
38:55.015 --> 38:57.740
Should I just bolt? No.

752
38:57.740 --> 39:01.505
Im Seong Min will sulk. Petty guy.

753
39:02.176 --> 39:04.426
Let's just endure it for one day.

754
39:06.515 --> 39:09.495
I think I saw this tree earlier.

755
39:09.495 --> 39:13.061
Where am I? They all look the same.

756
39:13.995 --> 39:16.795
Did I inhale too much smoke earlier?

757
39:16.795 --> 39:21.545
No. Let's just pick up one big log and go.

758
39:23.695 --> 39:26.325
That one. Just that one.

759
39:36.775 --> 39:39.137
It hurts! My ankle!

760
39:43.155 --> 39:46.395
It's been half an hour. Why isn't he back yet?

761
39:46.395 --> 39:49.935
He didn't go home, did he?

762
39:49.935 --> 39:53.572
This happens so often I'm getting PTSD.

763
39:53.572 --> 39:54.985
Me too.

764
39:56.811 --> 39:59.522
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu isn't like that.

765
39:59.522 --> 40:01.946
Shall we go look for him?

766
40:01.946 --> 40:03.346
Let's go.

767
40:04.495 --> 40:06.697
Please stay here.

768
40:08.595 --> 40:10.792
Be careful. Good luck.

769
40:10.792 --> 40:12.535
Il Gu!

770
40:13.652 --> 40:16.089
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu! - Il Gu!

771
40:20.578 --> 40:23.084
What?

772
40:23.084 --> 40:25.546
[The signal is weak] What's wrong...

773
40:27.290 --> 40:29.510
- Il Gu! - Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

774
40:29.510 --> 40:33.335
- Il Gu! - Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

775
40:33.335 --> 40:36.341
Il Gu! Staff...

776
40:37.813 --> 40:40.970
Why is there no signal?

777
40:40.970 --> 40:44.179
I want to live.

778
40:45.070 --> 40:47.282
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu! - Il Gu!

779
40:48.387 --> 40:52.515
- Squad Leader! - Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

780
40:52.515 --> 40:54.495
- Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju! - Why are you crying?

781
40:54.495 --> 40:56.329
Are you okay?

782
40:56.329 --> 41:00.007
Yes. I'm sorry. I lost my footing.

783
41:00.007 --> 41:01.755
Didn't you fall while running away?

784
41:01.755 --> 41:05.974
No. I was trying to get this firewood.

785
41:05.974 --> 41:09.745
- Can you get up? - I'll support you from behind.

786
41:11.195 --> 41:13.855
- Yes, thank you. - Careful.

787
41:13.855 --> 41:17.518
- Can you walk? - Watch your step here.

788
41:19.992 --> 41:22.715
What's taking them so long?

789
41:22.715 --> 41:24.445
Park Min Ju!

790
41:25.858 --> 41:27.983
Im Seong Min!

791
41:27.983 --> 41:29.425
Hold on.

792
41:30.355 --> 41:32.242
Wait, are they two together?

793
41:32.242 --> 41:34.235
Why did you come so far?

794
41:34.235 --> 41:37.339
Well, didn't you tell me to get firewood?

795
41:40.039 --> 41:43.593
Are you okay? Get up for now.

796
41:44.313 --> 41:48.595
- This looks really swollen. - That's not the injured foot.

797
41:48.595 --> 41:52.645
I'm sorry. What should I do?

798
41:54.556 --> 41:56.139
What should we do?

799
41:56.139 --> 41:59.202
I think I can walk by myself.

800
41:59.202 --> 42:00.895
At least wrap it with this.

801
42:00.895 --> 42:03.215
- Yes. Thank you. - I'm sorry.

802
42:03.215 --> 42:05.442
- No, it's fine. - Go slowly.

803
42:05.442 --> 42:07.275
Yes. Ugh, it hurts even more.

804
42:07.275 --> 42:08.855
- Hey, just go straight that way. - Yes.

805
42:08.855 --> 42:10.569
Take care.

806
42:11.435 --> 42:15.775
Choi Il Gu! Min Ju! Hey!

807
42:15.775 --> 42:18.435
Choi Il Gu!

808
42:18.435 --> 42:23.168
- Nursing Officer! I'm over here. - Choi Il Gu, you idiot.

809
42:23.168 --> 42:25.501
Nursing Officer!

810
42:25.501 --> 42:27.628
- Get on my back. - I'm fine.

811
42:27.628 --> 42:30.515
- We need to hurry, so get on my back. - I'm fine.

812
42:30.515 --> 42:33.456
If it gets worse, it's a loss of military power.

813
42:34.175 --> 42:36.121
Get on my back, quickly.

814
42:41.915 --> 42:45.285
It might be a bumpy ride, so hold on tight.

815
42:49.175 --> 42:50.869
Okay, watch your head.

816
42:53.227 --> 42:57.366
This is the first time I've been on a man's back, other than my dad's.

817
42:57.366 --> 43:00.141
I'm heavy, so don't overdo it.

818
43:00.141 --> 43:03.855
I have more muscle mass than I look.

819
43:04.832 --> 43:06.542
Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju,

820
43:06.542 --> 43:10.967
you must feel awkward being carried by someone.

821
43:10.967 --> 43:12.208
Yes.

822
43:13.627 --> 43:15.807
Don't always...

823
43:15.807 --> 43:18.453
try to carry everything on your own.

824
43:18.453 --> 43:20.177
Sometimes,

825
43:20.847 --> 43:24.037
it's okay to rely on others like this.

826
43:26.667 --> 43:29.432
Let's go camping together again next time.

827
43:30.227 --> 43:34.118
Sounds good. I'll tell Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

828
43:34.118 --> 43:36.942
Next time, just the two of us...

829
43:36.942 --> 43:40.287
- Are you okay? - I'm fine.

830
43:40.287 --> 43:43.079
- What did you just say? - It's nothing.

831
43:43.079 --> 43:44.107
Okay.

832
43:44.107 --> 43:45.327
- Hold on tight. - Okay.

833
43:45.327 --> 43:46.907
- I'll pick up the pace. - Okay.

834
43:46.907 --> 43:48.667
- But you know what? - What?

835
43:48.667 --> 43:52.042
You're lighter than I thought. Let's go all the way to the unit!

836
43:52.042 --> 43:53.668
Oh, stop it.

837
44:00.137 --> 44:01.725
We're here.

838
44:02.707 --> 44:04.317
Sergeant First Class Park.

839
44:06.060 --> 44:08.899
I'm sorry. I fell asleep without realizing.

840
44:09.847 --> 44:13.127
But will you be okay to drive?

841
44:13.127 --> 44:16.347
It feels much better than before. I'm fine.

842
44:16.347 --> 44:19.282
I'll go pack up the gear, so please wait here for a moment.

843
44:19.282 --> 44:20.771
- Okay. - Yes.

844
44:20.771 --> 44:23.064
- I'll be right back. - Okay.

845
44:45.227 --> 44:47.987
- All right, attention! - Attention!

846
44:47.987 --> 44:54.307
The division commander sent this pork belly to reward our 2nd Company's hard work.

847
44:54.307 --> 44:57.937
Most importantly, this is premium Handon.

848
45:00.531 --> 45:02.467
- Great. - Great!

849
45:02.467 --> 45:06.747
- Don't drink yourself under the table. Got it? - Yes, sir!

850
45:06.747 --> 45:08.997
Everyone, for our 2nd Company!

851
45:10.867 --> 45:12.910
- 2nd Company! - Cheers!

852
45:13.505 --> 45:17.327
- Put more meat on the grill. - Yes, sir.

853
45:33.901 --> 45:37.647
Hey, eat slowly, man. No one's going to steal it from you.

854
45:37.647 --> 45:39.147
Yes, sir.

855
45:41.287 --> 45:43.811
It would've been nice if Hyeon Uk was here.

856
45:43.811 --> 45:46.467
- He still has three days left. - Really?

857
45:46.467 --> 45:49.727
- Let's take good care of him when he's back. - Yes, sir.

858
45:49.727 --> 45:52.207
Is there any better health food than this?

859
45:52.207 --> 45:55.707
I'll wrap it in green onion salad and eat it properly.

860
45:55.707 --> 45:58.927
- Eat up. - This is delicious.

861
45:58.927 --> 46:00.481
It'd be nice if Se Gye were here too.

862
46:00.481 --> 46:01.553
It's so good.

863
46:01.553 --> 46:04.306
- I'll eat Se Gye's share too. - All right.

864
46:04.306 --> 46:07.227
- We're out of lettuce. - Keep eating. I'll go get some.

865
46:07.227 --> 46:10.907
- Thank you. - While you're at it, get some garlic too.

866
46:10.907 --> 46:13.807
Sure, sure. This guy...

867
46:13.807 --> 46:18.107
- Hey, grill it faster. Seriously. - Yes, sir.

868
46:18.107 --> 46:19.739
Eat this. Go on.

869
46:22.950 --> 46:25.490
Hey, why are the ribs taking so long?

870
46:26.367 --> 46:29.587
Grill them faster. Put some garlic on.

871
46:29.587 --> 46:33.001
Yoon Mo's going to get indigestion. Slow down, okay?

872
46:33.001 --> 46:35.811
I made some fried rice, so try it.

873
46:35.811 --> 46:37.464
Yes, thank you.

874
46:37.464 --> 46:42.219
Here's the pork fat fried rice you ordered.

875
46:42.219 --> 46:46.095
Why the sudden formal tone? Thank you.

876
46:46.095 --> 46:48.225
This looks amazing.

877
46:54.047 --> 46:55.232
Is something wrong?

878
46:55.232 --> 46:58.649
How is it? Look at that shine. Isn't it awesome?

879
46:58.649 --> 47:02.507
The company commander and I fried this ourselves with pork fat.

880
47:02.507 --> 47:06.487
But isn't all this grease bad for your health?

881
47:06.487 --> 47:10.946
What are you talking about? Pork fat is great!

882
47:10.946 --> 47:12.307
What's with him all of a sudden?

883
47:12.307 --> 47:15.991
It's high in unsaturated fatty acids, so it helps flush out pollutants...

884
47:15.991 --> 47:20.707
accumulated from air pollution and dust. It's also rich in vitamin E, which is...

885
47:20.707 --> 47:22.807
Il Gu.

886
47:22.807 --> 47:25.717
- Eat plenty of healthy food. - It's delicious.

887
47:26.937 --> 47:27.787
Eat up.

888
47:27.787 --> 47:31.107
- This is so good. - It's just delicious.

889
47:31.107 --> 47:34.967
- Enjoy the food, everyone! - Thank you for the meal.

890
47:34.967 --> 47:38.487
Domestic pork is a hundred times better than beef. Seriously.

891
47:38.487 --> 47:42.037
- We need to eat this regularly. - Regularly.

892
47:51.577 --> 47:56.084
- Hey, eat slowly. - Come again?

893
47:57.167 --> 47:59.127
Nothing. Eat a lot.

894
47:59.127 --> 48:03.290
- Have some, Sergeant Im. - Really?

895
48:03.290 --> 48:05.265
- Say ah. - Thanks.

896
48:05.265 --> 48:08.215
- Have this too. I was going to eat it. - Okay.

897
48:10.707 --> 48:13.327
- The battalion commander is here. - Attention!

898
48:13.327 --> 48:16.987
That's enough. Sit down. Keep eating. Relax.

899
48:16.987 --> 48:20.187
Battalion Commander, this way, please.

900
48:20.187 --> 48:23.422
Yes, thank you.

901
48:24.096 --> 48:25.367
I thought you said you couldn't make it.

902
48:25.367 --> 48:29.535
Well, I heard everyone having fun on my way home, so I stopped by.

903
48:29.535 --> 48:33.807
- Shall we fill our glasses first? - Yes, sir.

904
48:33.807 --> 48:38.595
First, a round of applause for the division commander for this event!

905
48:38.595 --> 48:40.657
[Eat your fill!] [7th Battalion, 2nd Co. Mission Success]

906
48:45.891 --> 48:47.087
And also,

907
48:47.087 --> 48:51.137
a round of applause for the Battalion Commander for his surprise visit!

908
48:53.350 --> 48:55.101
Byeon Hyeok Jin!

909
48:55.101 --> 48:58.117
- Byeon Hyeok Jin! - Byeon Hyeok Jin!

910
48:58.117 --> 48:59.871
Sir, a few words, please.

911
48:59.871 --> 49:04.991
Today is the day for the 2nd Company and its commander, so please say a word.

912
49:04.991 --> 49:06.459
Me?

913
49:07.091 --> 49:09.791
- The battalion commander is here. - Attention!

914
49:09.791 --> 49:13.451
That's enough. Sit down. Eat up. Relax.

915
49:13.451 --> 49:16.626
Battalion Commander, this way, please.

916
49:16.626 --> 49:19.180
Yes, thank you.

917
49:20.529 --> 49:21.886
I thought you said you couldn't make it.

918
49:21.886 --> 49:26.065
Well, I heard everyone having fun on my way home, so I stopped by.

919
49:26.065 --> 49:30.345
- Shall we fill our glasses first? - Yes, sir.

920
49:30.345 --> 49:34.722
First, a round of applause for the division commander for this event!

921
49:34.722 --> 49:37.023
[Eat your fill!] [7th Battalion, 2nd Co. Mission Success]

922
49:42.399 --> 49:43.605
And also,

923
49:43.605 --> 49:47.601
a round of applause for the Battalion Commander for his surprise visit!

924
49:49.758 --> 49:51.507
Byeon Hyeok Jin!

925
49:51.507 --> 49:54.711
- Byeon Hyeok Jin! - Byeon Hyeok Jin!

926
49:54.711 --> 49:56.311
Sir, a few words, please.

927
49:56.311 --> 50:01.471
Today is the day for the 2nd Company and its commander, so please say a word.

928
50:01.471 --> 50:03.605
Me? Yes, sir.

929
50:03.605 --> 50:07.347
A round of applause for Major-select

930
50:07.347 --> 50:10.806
Company Commander Cho Baek Ho!

931
50:12.271 --> 50:15.638
- Cho Baek Ho! - Cho Baek Ho!

932
50:15.638 --> 50:17.145
- Cho Baek Ho! - Cho Baek Ho!

933
50:17.145 --> 50:19.016
Quiet, quiet.

934
50:19.016 --> 50:23.741
First, you all worked so hard during the last Hoguk Exercise.

935
50:24.691 --> 50:27.365
I'm a company commander with many flaws,

936
50:27.971 --> 50:32.500
but I'm so grateful that you guys filled in my shortcomings.

937
50:32.500 --> 50:34.698
Enjoy the meat.

938
50:34.698 --> 50:39.002
If it's not enough, I'll buy more, so eat until you're full.

939
50:39.002 --> 50:40.851
- Got it? - Yes, sir!

940
50:40.851 --> 50:45.891
- Thanks. If I say "Chungseong," you know? - Yes, sir!

941
50:45.891 --> 50:50.875
- Chungseong! - Love you!

942
51:06.605 --> 51:11.944
♪ I must walk this endless path without getting tired ♪

943
51:11.944 --> 51:15.367
♪ Toward my tomorrow ♪

944
51:17.231 --> 51:22.496
♪ Every day, my cuts and scrapes make me stronger ♪

945
51:22.496 --> 51:25.919
♪ For my tomorrow ♪

946
51:26.871 --> 51:32.047
♪ When the hot sun sets ♪

947
51:32.047 --> 51:38.047
♪ My heart burns even hotter ♪

948
51:40.055 --> 51:45.155
♪ I'll keep running even if I'm out of breath ♪

949
51:45.155 --> 51:50.564
♪ I'll never give up, even in storms ♪

950
51:50.564 --> 51:56.599
♪ All the moments I cried and laughed ♪

951
51:56.599 --> 52:04.299
♪ will be the brightest days of my life ♪

952
52:09.918 --> 52:15.251
♪ Can you hear my roar? ♪

953
52:15.251 --> 52:20.139
♪ The brightest days of my life ♪

954
52:34.109 --> 52:36.031
Attention!

955
52:39.471 --> 52:44.591
We will now begin the morning roll call. First, any patients from last night?

956
52:44.591 --> 52:48.877
- I'm so hungover, Platoon Leader. - I think I'm going to throw up.

957
52:48.877 --> 52:54.877
Let's defeat that hangover with our spirit. Shout for five seconds!

958
53:01.723 --> 53:04.173
Hey, open the door.

959
53:09.610 --> 53:11.363
Chungseong!

960
53:20.697 --> 53:24.872
Once again, shout for five seconds!

961
53:31.811 --> 53:33.961
Make the reviewing stand shake!

962
53:33.961 --> 53:37.631
How can you defeat even an ant with that kind of spirit?

963
53:37.631 --> 53:41.680
Once again, shout for five seconds!

964
54:11.991 --> 54:17.796
We will now begin calisthenics. Start on my command!

965
54:17.796 --> 54:21.220
One, two, three, four.

966
54:26.171 --> 54:28.680
- She's arrived. - Okay.

967
54:31.897 --> 54:34.833
- Chungseong! - Chungseong!

968
54:35.831 --> 54:37.471
I'm Major Kim Ha Na.

969
54:37.471 --> 54:41.401
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin, the battalion commander. Please, sit.

970
54:49.551 --> 54:53.811
I've heard a lot about you from my colleague at the Corps Inspection Department.

971
54:53.811 --> 54:57.561
I doubt you heard anything good. It wasn't flattering, was it?

972
54:59.299 --> 55:01.301
I only heard good things.

973
55:01.301 --> 55:03.759
That's strange.

974
55:03.759 --> 55:08.015
First, I apologize for visiting without prior notice.

975
55:08.015 --> 55:11.713
It's fine. So, what brings you here?

976
55:13.689 --> 55:16.608
I'm here for a military-wide inventory audit.

977
55:16.608 --> 55:19.736
For the next two days, we'll inspect each company's warehouses, equipment,

978
55:19.736 --> 55:22.842
and overall facilities.

979
55:24.283 --> 55:26.299
An inventory audit?

980
55:27.533 --> 55:31.023
[Inventory Audit]

981
55:31.023 --> 55:36.025
A Corps inspector, and a major at that,

982
55:36.025 --> 55:38.752
coming down for an inventory audit in person...

983
55:38.752 --> 55:40.103
seems a bit unusual.

984
55:40.103 --> 55:45.083
It's proof that the higher-ups value this audit very much.

985
55:45.083 --> 55:48.423
Is that why you came by surprise?

986
55:48.423 --> 55:53.853
I was worried you'd feel that way, so I called to give you a heads-up.

987
56:00.123 --> 56:02.173
But you didn't answer...

988
56:03.277 --> 56:04.471
sir?

989
56:16.957 --> 56:19.376
- It's on me. - Thanks for the food.

990
56:19.376 --> 56:22.023
Here's the lettuce our beloved first sergeant likes.

991
56:22.023 --> 56:24.259
Since when do I like lettuce?

992
56:24.259 --> 56:27.012
Ma'am, is there some good news?

993
56:27.012 --> 56:31.471
- Yes, I have a group booking tomorrow. - For how many?

994
56:31.471 --> 56:34.823
A unit is having a dinner, so they ordered 100 servings.

995
56:34.823 --> 56:37.898
You can call it a day then.

996
56:37.898 --> 56:41.137
They said they need good liquor since the regimental commander is coming.

997
56:41.137 --> 56:45.443
They asked me to order it from their regular supplier for them.

998
56:45.443 --> 56:49.159
- What about the payment? - They'll pay for it with the dinner bill.

999
56:49.159 --> 56:53.185
- Really? - Yes, they even left a business card.

1000
56:53.185 --> 56:54.915
A business card?

1001
56:55.537 --> 56:59.211
"First Sergeant Yoo Seong Il, Administrative Support."

1002
57:00.303 --> 57:04.523
- Something smells fishy here. - What? I'll turn down the heat.

1003
57:04.523 --> 57:08.203
Not that smell. The smell of money.

1004
57:08.203 --> 57:11.139
The smell of money. I like that.

1005
57:11.139 --> 57:14.946
Speaking of which, I should transfer the money now.

1006
57:15.583 --> 57:17.189
- Hey, grill it well. - Yes, sir.

1007
57:17.189 --> 57:18.421
[Transferring 1,000,000 KRW]

1008
57:20.566 --> 57:22.296
Freeze!

1009
57:25.163 --> 57:27.563
- Choi Il Gu, you're late. - I'm sorry.

1010
57:27.563 --> 57:28.763
You're here?

1011
57:28.763 --> 57:32.741
Ma'am, did you check if that man was really a soldier?

1012
57:32.741 --> 57:35.247
Don't blindly trust anyone in uniform.

1013
57:35.247 --> 57:36.563
Right.

1014
57:36.563 --> 57:38.854
Don't decide on your own.

1015
57:38.854 --> 57:43.085
Call the Defense Help Call at 1303 to verify.

1016
57:43.085 --> 57:45.183
Defense Help Call 1303?

1017
57:45.183 --> 57:48.590
Yes. There are quite a few impostors these days.

1018
57:48.590 --> 57:51.057
And if you've been scammed,

1019
57:51.057 --> 57:54.623
report it to the police at 1394.

1020
57:54.623 --> 57:57.623
- I should call 1303. - Yes, hurry.

1021
57:57.623 --> 57:59.143
- Hello? - Go ahead and check.

1022
57:59.143 --> 58:05.067
Is this Defense Help Call? Someone came to my shop and ordered 100 servings...

1023
58:05.067 --> 58:09.263
Then he asked me to pay his supplier... What? He's not a soldier?

1024
58:09.263 --> 58:13.103
Hey, Choi Il Gu. It would've been a disaster if she had sent the money.

1025
58:13.103 --> 58:14.536
- Seriously. - Exactly.

1026
58:14.536 --> 58:18.910
When something smells fishy, you have to verify it first, right?

1027
58:21.223 --> 58:23.543
- What's wrong? - What's that smell?

1028
58:23.543 --> 58:25.232
What smell?

1029
58:27.216 --> 58:29.283
You were late, so the meat's all burnt!

1030
58:29.283 --> 58:32.123
I'm sorry. I was busy running an errand for the command sergeant major.

1031
58:32.123 --> 58:34.363
- Grill it. - Yes, I'll grill it.

1032
58:34.363 --> 58:36.096
- Everyone together! - Yes!

1033
58:36.096 --> 58:38.643
- Cheers! - Cheers!

1034
58:38.643 --> 58:41.064
- Do it right! - Yes, sir!
